From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:13:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP: keep the configured width on 5/6 GHz if the 20/40 MHz
 scan fails

Before enabling a 40 MHz (or wider) BSS, hostapd scans the affected
channels for overlapping BSSes. If the driver refuses the scan with
-EBUSY, ap_ht40_scan_retry() tries again once a second, and after 15
attempts brings the BSS up at 20 MHz.

On a single wiphy with several radios (e.g. ath12k with a 2.4, 5 and
6 GHz radio) only one radio can scan at a time, so while another radio
scans (ACS, its own coexistence scan, a station scan), the 5 GHz or 6 GHz
radio can run out of retries and comes up at 20 MHz, although nothing
on the channel asked for that.

On 5/6 GHz the result of that scan can only swap the primary and
secondary channel: check_40mhz_5g() returns 1 or 2 for any valid channel
pair and never disallows 40 MHz. Skipping it is what noscan=1 already
does. So when the scan cannot be run there, keep the configured channel
width and bring the BSS up as configured. 2.4 GHz still falls back to
20 MHz, since there the scan can forbid 40 MHz.

Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
 src/ap/hw_features.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/hw_features.c b/src/ap/hw_features.c
index 9db7eb1e1..681d2345b 100644
--- a/src/ap/hw_features.c
+++ b/src/ap/hw_features.c
@@ -598,6 +598,18 @@ static void ap_ht40_scan_retry(void *eloop_data, void *user_data)
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * On 5/6 GHz the scan can only make us swap the primary and secondary
+	 * channel (check_40mhz_5g() never disallows 40 MHz there), so without
+	 * it keep the configured width, as noscan=1 does.
+	 */
+	if (iface->current_mode->mode == HOSTAPD_MODE_IEEE80211A) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+			   "Failed to request a scan of neighboring BSSes, keeping the configured channel width");
+		hostapd_setup_interface_complete(iface, 0);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 		   "Failed to request a scan in device, bringing up in HT20 mode");
 	hostapd_set_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx(iface->conf, 0);
